@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Share Upload Orchestration
  "Two-phase share workflow: ensure blob exists on the server, then ensure link endpoints via links.Service."

  Provides:
    - share.Uploader @source("symbol:Uploader")
    - share.Linker @source("symbol:Linker")
    - share.Service @source("symbol:Service")
    - share.NewService @source("symbol:NewService")
    - share.Request @source("symbol:Request")
    - share.Result @source("symbol:Result")
    - share.Service.Share @source("symbol:Share")

  Consumes:
    - config.Share
    - remote.RemoteFS
    - remote.ManifestStore
    - links.Service
    - domain.ResolveSharePath

  Invariants:
    - Share MUST hash locally, upload only when the blob is absent from the manifest, then link
    - ensureBlob MUST record blob size and uploaded_at in the manifest after successful rsync
    - Result MUST include long and short URLs derived from the share store URL

  OutOfScope:
    - Remote-link mutations without upload (owned by the links package)
    - Deploy rsync of build trees (future internal/deploy)

  Scenario (happy-path): Link-only share
    Given blob bytes already present in the remote manifest
    When Share runs for a new object path
    Then Uploaded is false and links are created

  Scenario (happy-path): Upload then link
    Given a new blob hash not in the manifest
    When Share runs
    Then the blob is rsynced, recorded, and endpoints are linked

  Scenario (negative): Missing local file
    Given a non-existent file path
    When Share runs
    Then it returns an error before remote mutation
